# arm64 override of genstage/live/hardened/etc/audit/rules.d/10-base.rules —
# kept in sync with ../audit.rules per that file's header comment (auditd
# loads audit.rules directly and never runs augenrules, so this copy is only
# a fallback for the day augenrules --load is used). Full rationale for the
# syscall-list change and the dropped b32 line: see ../audit.rules.

# First rule - delete all
# This is to clear out old rules, so we don't append to them.
-D

# Feel free to add below this line. See auditctl man page

# aarch64 only — see ../audit.rules for why b32 is dropped and why
# open/fstat/dup2/stat became openat/newfstatat/dup3.
-a exit,never -F arch=b64 -S read -S write -S openat -S newfstatat -S mmap -S brk -S munmap -S nanosleep -S fcntl -S close -S dup3 -S rt_sigaction

# The following rule would cause the capture of all systems not caught above.
# -a exit,always -S all

# Increase the buffers to survive stress events
-b 8192

# vim:ft=conf:
